# Skyrmion collapse

Alberto D. Verga — arXiv:1409.0256v2 [cond-mat.mes-hall]

## Coupled electron--spin dynamics (Sec. II)

The itinerant electrons obey a tight-binding Schrödinger equation on a square
lattice; the localized texture $\mathbf{S}(\mathbf{r},t)$, $|\mathbf{S}|=1$, obeys
the Landau--Lifshitz equation with spin-transfer torque from the electron spin
density $\mathbf{s}$ and a polarization (b-)field:

$$
\partial_t \mathbf{S} \;=\; -\,\mathbf{S}\times \mathbf{H}_{\mathrm{eff}}
\;+\; \text{(STT from }\mathbf{s}\text{)} \;+\; d\,\text{(exchange dissipation)} .
$$

The magnetic energy is the classical Heisenberg exchange (no DMI):

$$
H_S \;=\; \frac{J}{2}\int (\nabla \mathbf{S})^2\, d^2r
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad
H \;=\; J\!\!\sum_{\langle ij\rangle}\!\bigl(1-\mathbf{S}_i\!\cdot\!\mathbf{S}_j\bigr).
$$

Without dissipation the system conserves $|\mathbf{S}|=1$ and the topological
charge $Q(t)$.

## Belavin--Polyakov skyrmion (Sec. IV, Eq. 8 / lines 428--429)

Stereographic projection onto the complex plane, $w=w(z)$, $z=x+iy$:

$$
w_0(z) \;=\; \frac{z}{\lambda},
\qquad
S_z=\frac{\lambda^2-r^2}{\lambda^2+r^2},\;\;
S_x+iS_y=\frac{2\lambda\,(x+iy)}{\lambda^2+r^2}.
$$

Exchange energy and charge (scale-invariant — independent of $\lambda$):

$$
E_{\mathrm{xc}} \;=\; 4\pi J,
\qquad
Q \;=\; \frac{1}{4\pi}\int \mathbf{S}\cdot(\partial_x\mathbf{S}\times\partial_y\mathbf{S})\,d^2r \;=\; \pm 1 .
$$

Lattice topological charge (Berg--Lüscher solid angle of each spin triangle):

$$
Q \;=\; \frac{1}{4\pi}\sum_{\triangle}\Omega_{\triangle},
\qquad
\tan\!\Big(\tfrac{\Omega}{2}\Big)=
\frac{\mathbf{S}_a\cdot(\mathbf{S}_b\times\mathbf{S}_c)}
{1+\mathbf{S}_a\!\cdot\!\mathbf{S}_b+\mathbf{S}_b\!\cdot\!\mathbf{S}_c+\mathbf{S}_c\!\cdot\!\mathbf{S}_a}.
$$

## Self-similar finite-time collapse (Sec. IV, Eqs. 15--17)

Perturbative core shrinking under the current:

$$
\lambda(t) \;=\; \frac{\lambda_0}{\sqrt{1+(s_0 t)^2}},
\qquad s_0 \sim n_e B_p .
$$

Self-similar ansatz near the singularity $t\to t^*$:

$$
w(\mathbf{r},t) \;=\; (t^*-t)^{-\alpha}\, f\!\Big(\frac{r}{(t^*-t)^{\beta}}\Big).
$$

Dimensional balance of the driven Landau--Lifshitz equation
(time-derivative $\sim (t^*-t)^{-\alpha-1}$; exchange $\nabla^2 w \sim (t^*-t)^{-\alpha-2\beta}$;
STT nonlinearity $w^2 \sim (t^*-t)^{-2\alpha}$) gives the $2\times2$ system

$$
-\alpha-1=-\alpha-2\beta \;\Rightarrow\; \beta=\tfrac12,
\qquad
-\alpha-1=-2\alpha \;\Rightarrow\; \alpha=1 .
$$

$$
\boxed{\;\alpha=1,\qquad \beta=\tfrac12\;}\qquad\text{(Eq. 17)}
$$

Collapse time: $t^* \sim \lambda/(s_0 a)$. At $t=t^*$ the characteristic skyrmion
size vanishes; the exact self-similar solution (Eq. 24/25) again has energy
$\propto 4\pi J$ and charge $Q=1$ up to the singular instant, after which a
single-spin flip changes $Q$ on the lattice.
